  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "OffsetPerRowOrCol::apply",
    "file": "librawspeed/src/librawspeed/common/DngOpcodes.cpp",
    "description": "Heap OOB read is caused by missing bounds validation between image dimensions and opcode delta table length for DeltaPerColumn/DeltaPerRow opcodes. OffsetPerRowOrCol::apply indexes deltaI/deltaF with S::select(x,y) (x for SelectX, y for SelectY) for every pixel, but never checks that the delta array has at least width (or height) elements. A crafted opcode with too-short deltaF_count passes parsing, then apply() reads past vector bounds.",
    "conditions": "Input must be a DNG/TIFF parsed by DngDecoder::handleMetadata with OPCODELIST1 (or stage2 OPCODELIST2) containing opcode 11 (DeltaPerColumn, SelectX) in this PoV. After decodeData, applyOpCodes runs and iterates all pixels; if deltaF_count < image width (for SelectX) or < image height (for SelectY), S::select(x,y) eventually exceeds delta vector size, triggering heap-buffer-overflow read in OffsetPerRowOrCol::apply."
  },
